From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:08:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ppe: release quarantined flow egress references

Quarantined rows retain their hardware leases until teardown, but are
excluded from topology and statistics callbacks. Release their software
egress reference alongside the path and accounting references so a failed
hardware retirement cannot block DSA port unregistration.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
@@ -2691,6 +2691,10 @@ static void ppe_ft_flow_quarantine(struc
 	ppe_ft_path_put(flow);
 	ppe_flow_account_put(&flow->rx_account);
 	ppe_flow_account_put(&flow->tx_account);
+	if (flow->egress_dev) {
+		dev_put(flow->egress_dev);
+		flow->egress_dev = NULL;
+	}
 
 	ret = ppe_flow_entry_matches(ft->ppe_dev, flow->index, &flow->entry);
 	if (!ret)
